[stderr] | Onboarding/tutorial and player guidance | explicit | Required capability. | Required first-release capabilities |
[stderr] | Save/load/resume, persistence, migrations, data-loss recovery | explicit | Direct shared and first-release requirement. | Shared; required capabilities |
[stderr] | Responsive 2D rendering, input adapters, browser performance | explicit | 2D, responsive web, keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad. | Characteristics; web requirements |
[stderr] | PWA installation, offline assets/content, cache/update safety | explicit | Direct PWA requirement. | PWA requirements |
[stderr] | Android/iOS packaging, touch/orientation, mobile budgets | explicit | Both targets named. | Android/iPhone requirements |
[stderr] | Accessibility: controls, text, captions, visual settings, focus/reduced motion | explicit | Direct shared requirement. | Shared requirements |
[stderr] | Localisation and language-content pipeline | explicit | Localisation named; languages unknown. | Cross-platform decisions |
[stderr] | Original visual/audio feedback and asset pipeline | explicit | Feedback and art direction named. | Required capabilities; art direction |
[stderr] | Content delivery/versioning/validation/rollback communication | implied | Curated content and updates need controlled release. | Content delivery; PWA requirements |
[stderr] | Crash diagnostics, error boundaries, recovery UI, support triage | explicit | Crash reporting and player recovery are direct. | Shared; required capabilities |
[stderr] | Quality: correctness, adjudication, persistence, offline/update, accessibility, compatibility, performance | implied | Each promise needs validation beyond screens. | Targets; shared requirements |
[stderr] | Privacy/security, consent, minimisation, retention/deletion | explicit | Privacy required; accounts/diagnostics may process data. | Constraints; cross-platform decisions |
[stderr] | Account identity, remote sync, conflicts | requires-decision | Named but no policy or local-state relationship. | Required capabilities; data policy |
[stderr] | Multiplayer safety, reporting, moderation, community operations | requires-decision | Named but conflicts with single-player and lacks mode/policy. | Characteristics; required capabilities |
[stderr] | Live-service status, incident response, event tooling | requires-decision | Named while events are deferred, operating model absent. | Required/deferred capabilities |
[stderr] | Purchases, catalogue, entitlements, refunds, compliance | requires-decision | Named while monetisation deferred, policy absent. | Required/deferred capabilities |
[stderr] | Advanced analytics | deferred | Explicit later scope; crash diagnostics remain required. | Later capabilities |
[stderr] | Seasonal/live events and player-created/shared content | deferred | Explicit later scope. | Later capabilities |
[stderr] | Engine/framework, vendors, CI/CD, costs, support matrix/budgets | requires-decision | No technical/testable baseline authorized. | Constraints; target requirements |
[stderr] | Campaign/story/battle content | requires-decision | Generic user outcome conflicts with specific trivia request. | Users; first useful session |
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Conclusions, assumptions, and gates
[stderr] 
[stderr] The minimal release depends on quiz shell, authored validated content,
[stderr] round/adjudication/score rules, local persistence, rendering/input,
[stderr] accessibility, original feedback, target delivery, recovery, release controls,
[stderr] and focused QA. Editorial tooling is required as a candidate enabling discipline,
[stderr] but workflow/operations cadence is not selected.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Safe assumptions: independently authored expression; shared core with adapted
[stderr] inputs; locally available approved content supports a basic session; confirmed
[stderr] local saves are protected where storage permits; approved remote features fail
[stderr] visibly; and diagnostics minimise personal data. These do not approve a vendor,
[stderr] backend, account model, retention policy, or fact-licensing arrangement.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Human approval is required for campaign/battle framing; connected/account/sync
[stderr] scope; multiplayer/community safety; commerce; question sources/licensing/bank
[stderr] size; languages/audio quantities; target matrices/budgets; stack/vendors;
[stderr] store/legal policy; and live-operations ownership. Decision-gated systems must
[stderr] not block the single-player trivia core or introduce RPG scope.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Reference boundary
[stderr] 
[stderr] The Athletic and QuizUp may inform only football-topic breadth, varied quiz
[stderr] formats, and the broad goal of short trivia sessions. They never authorize
[stderr] copied brands, questions/wording, assets, layouts, screen composition, audio,
[stderr] social copy, interaction choreography, or other distinctive expression. All
[stderr] content, mechanics expression, UI, visual, and audio work must be original.
[stderr] # 01 — Game identity
[stderr] 
[stderr] **Status:** first-release game layer, before genre-specific content planning.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Pillars and stable design units
[stderr] 
[stderr] | ID | Unit | Commitment |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | GAME-001 | Fast football knowledge | Enter a themed trivia round and make repeated answer decisions in a quick mobile-friendly session. |
[stderr] | GAME-002 | Fair, legible adjudication | Every question has an answer rule and communicates result, score change, and feedback accessibly. |
[stderr] | GAME-003 | Momentum without punishment | Scores/streaks create tension; wrong answers are recoverable and results are understandable. |
[stderr] | GAME-004 | Curated variety | Authored categories, formats, difficulty, and anti-repetition make short sessions fresh. |
[stderr] | GAME-005 | Trustworthy return play | Local progress, save/resume, approved offline content, settings, and recovery support safe return. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Fantasy, loop, sessions, and progression
[stderr] 
[stderr] Player fantasy: be the person who spots the football answer before the clock,
[stderr] builds a run of confident calls, and improves their knowledge. Verbs: **read or
[stderr] listen**, **recall**, **select or enter**, **confirm**, **review**, **continue**.
[stderr] Loop: choose/receive theme → consume prompt → submit → adjudication and
[stderr] accessible feedback → update score/streak/progress → next suitable prompt →
[stderr] finish or safely resume. Sessions are short, interruptible rounds with
[stderr] onboarding first, an objective, question sequence, results, and saved return
[stderr] state. Progression promises broader knowledge and local milestones, not levels,
[stderr] equipment, traversal, or combat power.
[stderr] 
[stderr] The emotional arc is curiosity, competence, mounting stakes, then celebration
[stderr] or useful recovery. Audience: casual adult football-interested players using
[stderr] touch, keyboard, mouse, gamepad, captions, adjustable text, and visual settings.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## game-design-signals
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Signal | Classification and evidence | Design consequence |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | Archetype | Football trivia/puzzle/turn-based card-like quiz; source names trivia, formats, and checked puzzle/card/board/turn-based. | Questions, rounds, answers, and results—not action/adventure content. |
[stderr] | Primary activity | Recall/recognise and answer; source names validation and feedback. | Input, adjudication, explanations, and score rules. |
[stderr] | Session model | Quick mobile sessions with local progress/save. | Short lifecycle and interruption-safe state. |
[stderr] | Knowledge source | Curated editorial football bank. | Provenance, review, categories, difficulty, refresh. |
[stderr] | Social model | Single-player; multiplayer is undefined. | No opponents, matchmaking, chat, co-op, rankings, or social graph in core. |
[stderr] | Creative intensity | Editorial questions/feedback high; fictional narrative low. | Question tooling, not lore/character pipeline. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Candidate module decision record
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Module | Decision | Rationale |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | Question provenance/categories/formats/difficulty/answers/explanations | Selected | Necessary for curated themed trivia and validation. |
[stderr] | Round/mode rules, scoring/streaks, results, anti-repetition, milestones | Selected | Named or necessary for replayable short sessions. |
[stderr] | Onboarding, accessibility, input, save/recovery, web/PWA/mobile delivery | Selected | Explicit shared and target requirements. |
[stderr] | Editorial refresh and validation tooling | Selected candidate | Factual curated content needs correction and quality controls; cadence awaits approval. |
[stderr] | Accounts/sync, multiplayer safety, live ops, commerce | Requires decision | Named but conflicts with core and lacks policy. |
[stderr] | RPG world/party/quests/combat/jobs/enemies/bosses/equipment/locations | Rejected | Not evidenced; generic campaign/battle wording is a decision, not scope. |
[stderr] | Builder economy/construction; racing physics; match simulation; platforming | Rejected | No player-activity evidence. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] Completion is an accessible results state with score, streak outcome, and next
[stderr] step; an interruption becomes safe resumable state where supported. Narrative,
[stderr] competitive-rank, and seasonal completion are outside first release unless an
[stderr] approval decision changes this identity.
[stderr] # 01 — Creative direction
[stderr] 
[stderr] **Inputs:** [`INITIAL.md`](../INITIAL.md) and
[stderr] [`PROJECT_BRIEF.md`](../PROJECT_BRIEF.md). This is the early creative north star
[stderr] for content, feature, art, audio, and implementation work.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Narrative/gameplay framing and voice
[stderr] 
[stderr] The player is a quick-thinking football devotee on a short “matchday knowledge”
[stderr] challenge: recognise a clue, make a confident call, and build momentum through a
[stderr] themed round. The play space is an original abstract broadcast studio, not a
[stderr] named stadium, club, league, publisher, or existing product. The goal is to
[stderr] finish a curated round with a strong score/streak and learn from clear feedback.
[stderr] 
[stderr] The engagement arc is invitation, first confidence, rising streak tension, a
[stderr] decisive final prompt, then a clear celebration or learning-oriented result.
[stderr] First-release content needs questions, themes, answer explanations/feedback,
[stderr] local milestones, and results/completion states. It needs no fictional
[stderr] characters, lore, RPG party, quests, bosses, combat, or narrative ending. The
[stderr] brief's campaign/battle contradiction requires approval before such content is
[stderr] produced.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Writing is precise, lively, inclusive, and fact-first: short prompts,
[stderr] unambiguous instructions, plain-language adjudication, and celebratory but
[stderr] non-taunting feedback. Authors avoid stereotypes, unreviewed claims, and
[stderr] imitation of reference publications.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Visual and audio intent
[stderr] 
[stderr] Visual direction: original modern football-broadcast graphics, bold accessible
[stderr] category colours, large score numerals, readable typography, disciplined card
[stderr] geometry, clear answer states, and restrained motion. Prompt hierarchy comes
[stderr] first, answer action second, score/streak third. Colour is never the only cue;
[stderr] the system supports adjustable text, focus, reduced motion, high contrast,
[stderr] captions, and responsive portrait-first layouts. Use original abstract pitch
[stderr] lines, stat blocks, signal sweeps, and celebration shapes—never real club,
[stderr] competition, broadcaster, publisher, or QuizUp marks, kit designs, screenshots,
[stderr] or screen composition.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Audio direction: an original restrained percussive entry bed; distinct correct,
[stderr] incorrect, streak, optional urgency, and completion cues; and a warm short
[stderr] results sting. Bright electronic percussion, claps, soft brass-like synth
[stderr] accents, and abstract crowd energy are allowed; sampled or imitated chants,
[stderr] anthems, broadcasts, clubs, or games are not. Essential meaning always has
[stderr] text/visual alternatives plus volume, mute, and caption/description options.
[stderr] Exact cue quantities/durations/loop policy remain production decisions.
[stderr] 
[stderr] The Athletic and QuizUp are functional references only: no copying of branding,
[stderr] questions, wording, copy, art, audio, layouts, flow choreography, or distinctive
[stderr] interactions. All expression is independently authored.
