[stderr] +# 02 — Game design bible
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Status:** original first-release design proposal derived from the discovery
[stderr] +classification. It deliberately implements a football-trivia game, not an RPG
[stderr] +or football match simulation.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Selected modules and production units
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Module | ID | First-release design unit | Production mode |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| `quiz-content` | GAME-001 | Question cards carry an original prompt, category, format, difficulty, answer rule, explanation, provenance/review status, and repeat eligibility. | editorial-schema |
[stderr] +| `round-rules` | GAME-002 | A themed short round sequences eligible cards, resolves answers deterministically, applies a score/streak rule, and ends in a results state. | rules-and-state |
[stderr] +| `player-experience` | GAME-003 | Onboarding, accessible feedback, pause/resume, settings, and recovery make the short session understandable and safely interruptible. | interaction-and-accessibility |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Boundaries
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The selected modules support the GAME-001 through GAME-005 identity pillars:
[stderr] +fast football knowledge, fair adjudication, recoverable momentum, curated
[stderr] +variety, and trustworthy return play. Candidate editorial refresh tooling is a
[stderr] +supporting workflow for `quiz-content`, not a promise of live service.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Rejected modules remain out of scope: fictional world, party, combat, quests,
[stderr] +bosses, equipment, builder economy, racing physics, match simulation,
[stderr] +platforming, matchmaking, chat, rankings, and social graph. Account, remote
[stderr] +sync, multiplayer safety, commerce, and live operations require separate human
[stderr] +approval before selection.
[stderr] diff --git a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md
