[stderr] --- /dev/null
[stderr] +++ b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md
[stderr] @@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
[stderr] +# 02 — Game design bible
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Status:** original first-release design proposal derived from the discovery
[stderr] +classification. It deliberately implements a football-trivia game, not an RPG
[stderr] +or football match simulation.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Selected modules and production units
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Module | ID | First-release design unit | Production mode |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| `quiz-content` | GAME-001 | Question cards carry an original prompt, category, format, difficulty, answer rule, explanation, provenance/review status, and repeat eligibility. | editorial-schema |
[stderr] +| `round-rules` | GAME-002 | A themed short round sequences eligible cards, resolves answers deterministically, applies a score/streak rule, and ends in a results state. | rules-and-state |
[stderr] +| `player-experience` | GAME-003 | Onboarding, accessible feedback, pause/resume, settings, and recovery make the short session understandable and safely interruptible. | interaction-and-accessibility |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Boundaries
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The selected modules support the identity pillars of fast football knowledge,
[stderr] +fair adjudication, recoverable momentum, curated variety, and trustworthy return
[stderr] +play. Candidate editorial refresh tooling is a supporting workflow for
[stderr] +`quiz-content`, not a promise of live service.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Rejected modules remain out of scope: fictional world, party, combat, quests,
[stderr] +bosses, equipment, builder economy, racing physics, match simulation,
[stderr] +platforming, matchmaking, chat, rankings, and social graph. Account, remote
[stderr] +sync, multiplayer safety, commerce, and live operations require separate human
[stderr] +approval before selection.
[stderr] diff --git a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md
[stderr] new file mode 100644
[stderr] index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..c5f7328dcf4019f6ded1b7ab82cb9ab117f427a8
[stderr] --- /dev/null
[stderr] +++ b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md
[stderr] @@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
[stderr] +# 04 — Asset direction
[stderr] +
[stderr] +All asset groups use the original abstract broadcast-studio direction established
[stderr] +in `01-creative-direction.md`; they must not reproduce clubs, competitions,
[stderr] +broadcasters, The Athletic, QuizUp, kit designs, screenshots, or layouts.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| ID | Asset group | Direction and accessibility boundary |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| ASSET-001 | Category and round graphics | Original bold category fields, abstract pitch lines, stat blocks, and signal sweeps; labels and shapes carry meaning beyond colour. |
[stderr] +| ASSET-002 | Answer and score feedback | Original correct/incorrect/streak/completion state motifs with text, icon, and motion-reduced alternatives. |
[stderr] +| ASSET-003 | Install and responsive shell art | Original neutral app-mark and scalable studio surfaces; no real team, competition, or reference-product marks. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Asset quantities, file formats, and final delivery budgets remain pending target
[stderr] +and packaging decisions. Each asset requires provenance and human creative
[stderr] +review before production use.
[stderr] diff --git a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md
[stderr] new file mode 100644
[stderr] index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..80b9199a22884f3ba1a05ef471920526a4e70852
[stderr] --- /dev/null
[stderr] +++ b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md
[stderr] @@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
[stderr] +# 04 — Audio direction
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Audio is original, optional, captioned/described where it conveys state, and
[stderr] +always paired with a visual/text equivalent. No chant, anthem, broadcast,
[stderr] +club, or game imitation is permitted.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| ID | Cue group | Intent |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| AUDIO-001 | Entry and round bed | Restrained, low-distraction electronic percussion with abstract crowd-energy texture; optional and volume-controlled. |
[stderr] +| AUDIO-002 | Answer and streak feedback | Brief distinct correct, incorrect, and streak cues using claps and soft brass-like synth accents without sampled sports expression. |
[stderr] +| AUDIO-003 | Results and completion | Warm, short celebratory sting that supports rather than replaces the readable results state. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Final durations, quantities, loudness targets, loop policy, and generated-cue
[stderr] +selection need production approval; no audio is generated by this plan.
