@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+# 02 — Game design bible
+
+**Status:** original first-release design proposal derived from the discovery
+classification. It deliberately implements a football-trivia game, not an RPG
+or football match simulation.
+
+## Selected modules and production units
+
+| Module | ID | First-release design unit | Production mode |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `quiz-content` | GAME-001 | Question cards carry an original prompt, category, format, difficulty, answer rule, explanation, provenance/review status, and repeat eligibility. | editorial-schema |
+| `round-rules` | GAME-002 | A themed short round sequences eligible cards, resolves answers deterministically, applies a score/streak rule, and ends in a results state. | rules-and-state |
+| `player-experience` | GAME-003 | Onboarding, accessible feedback, pause/resume, settings, and recovery make the short session understandable and safely interruptible. | interaction-and-accessibility |
+
+## Boundaries
+
+The selected modules support the GAME-001 through GAME-005 identity pillars:
+fast football knowledge, fair adjudication, recoverable momentum, curated
+variety, and trustworthy return play. Candidate editorial refresh tooling is a
