NFR-0004\",\"NFR-0005\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Settings and feedback contracts cover text, contrast, motion, caption visibility, audio controls, preference failure, and reset confirmation while retaining unapproved audio and localisation scope.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0010\",\"IMP-0006\",\"IMP-0022\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/app/settings/\",\"src/app/accessibility/\",\"tests/app/accessibility/\"],\"data\":[\"local preference model and caption state\"],\"api\":[\"settings and accessible-status API\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"audio asset creation\",\"locale selection\",\"cloud preferences\",\"WCAG conformance claim\"],\"verification\":\"Tests cover reduced motion, non-colour state text, preference-write failure, and reset isolation from campaign saves.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0002, GATE-0003, and GATE-0004 remain explicit implementation and release gates.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"ready_for_authoring\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0025\",\"title\":\"Define recoverable empty, error, and destructive UI states\",\"domain\":\"ui\",\"targets\":[\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0006\",\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0003\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Bounded UI state contracts explain empty content, invalid actions, save failure, recovery, diagnostics, and selected-slot deletion with focus-safe confirmation.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0006\",\"IMP-0009\",\"IMP-0021\",\"IMP-0022\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/app/recovery/\",\"src/app/dialogs/\",\"tests/app/recovery/\"],\"data\":[\"recovery and confirmation view state\"],\"api\":[\"recoverable error and confirmation API\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"diagnostic transport\",\"automatic destructive repair\",\"cache lifecycle\",\"remote support\"],\"verification\":\"Fixtures prove destructive actions start on Cancel, invalid actions preserve state, and recovery exposes legal next actions.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0003 and GATE-0005 remain explicit for storage policy and diagnostics transport.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"ready_for_authoring\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0026\",\"title\":\"Add SHARD-03 accessibility and input integration evidence\",\"domain\":\"tests\",\"targets\":[\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0007\",\"REQ-0009\",\"REQ-0010\",\"NFR-0004\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Deterministic contract fixtures cross-check session, shell, input, settings, and recovery boundaries while reserving browser/device matrix evidence for the approved release gate.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0021\",\"IMP-0022\",\"IMP-0023\",\"IMP-0024\",\"IMP-0025\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"tests/app/accessibility-integration/\",\"docs/ui-handoff.md\"],\"data\":[\"accessibility and input evidence matrix\"],\"api\":[\"documented SHARD-04 handoff\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"real-device certification\",\"PWA service worker\",\"product assets\",\"release approval\"],\"verification\":\"Structural review finds every SHARD-03 contract covered once and preserves all retained gates.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0002, GATE-0003, and GATE-0004 remain unresolved.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"ready_for_authoring\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0027\",\"title\":\"Define PWA manifest and install eligibility boundary\",\"domain\":\"pwa\",\"targets\":[\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0011\",\"NFR-0001\",\"NFR-0009\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A manifest and install-readiness contract identifies original public metadata, icons as reserved assets, and explicit unsupported-state behaviour without claiming browser support or store distribution.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0022\",\"IMP-0026\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/platform/web/pwa/manifest*\",\"tests/platform/pwa/manifest*\"],\"data\":[\"PWA manifest and install state\"],\"api\":[\"install eligibility API\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"store submission\",\"native package\",\"copied branding\",\"supported-browser claim\"],\"verification\":\"Schema and negative fixtures reject incomplete manifest data and represent unavailable installation safely.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0002 and GATE-0007 remain for browser matrix and original visual assets.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"ready_for_authoring\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0028\",\"title\":\"Specify safe service-worker cache, update, and offline recovery lifecycle\",\"domain\":\"pwa\",\"targets\":[\"pwa\",\"web\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0011\",\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0003\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A service-worker lifecycle keeps immutable release cache separate from saves, applies updates only at a safe session boundary, and retains a known-good cache after refresh failure.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0006\",\"IMP-0021\",\"IMP-0027\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/platform/web/pwa/{worker,cache,update}*\",\"tests/platform/pwa/lifecycle*\"],\"data\":[\"cache version and update state\"],\"api\":[\"safe update and offline status API\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"save migration\",\"remote sync\",\"background data collection\",\"host deployment\"],\"verification\":\"Fixtures cover offline launch, failed refresh, cache eviction boundary, and confirmed-save update timing.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0002 and GATE-0005 remain for browser/storage policy and security review.\",\"complexity\":\"high\",\"status\":\"ready_for_authoring\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0029\",\"title\":\"Define release configuration, artifact integrity, and local diagnostics checks\",\"domain\":\"release\",\"targets\":[\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"NFR-0006\",\"NFR-0011\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Bounded release checks validate public configuration, artifact provenance, secret exclusion, local diagnostic redaction, and a candidate evidence record without contacting a host.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0008\",\"IMP-0009\",\"IMP-0028\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"scripts/release-check*\",\"docs/security-and-provenance.md\",\"tests/release/checks*\"],\"data\":[\"candidate evidence record\"],\"api\":[\"release-check result schema\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"secrets\",\"third-party scan claim\",\"deployment\",\"remote diagnostics\"],\"verification\":\"Positive and malformed configuration fixtures, artifact scan fixtures, and redaction checks are deterministic.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0005 and GATE-0007 remain for policy, security, and provenance review.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"ready_for_authoring\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0030\",\"title\":\"Specify performance and compatibility evidence collection boundary\",\"domain\":\"quality\",\"targets\":[\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"NFR-0001\",\"NFR-0009\",\"NFR-0011\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A repeatable evidence harness records candidate, environment, method, result, and exceptions while refusing pass claims without approved budgets and device/browser matrix.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0023\",\"IMP-0028\",\"IMP-0029\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"tests/performance/\",\"docs/performance-evidence.md\"],\"data\":[\"measurement and compatibility evidence template\"],\"api\":[\"quality evidence schema\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"invented performance result\",\"certification claim\",\"unapproved thresholds\",\"production monitoring\"],\"verification\":\"Schema fixtures reject incomplete evidence and label unapproved matrix/budget checks not run.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0002 and GATE-0005 remain for approved targets, budgets, and policy.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"ready_for_authoring\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0031\",\"title\":\"Document player recovery and operator release/rollback boundary\",\"domain\":\"documentation\",\"targets\":[\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0003\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Player and operator documentation describes local save/cache separation, update recovery, rollback holds, privacy controls, and evidence responsibilities without asserting a release occurred.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0025\",\"IMP-0028\",\"IMP-0029\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"docs/{player-guide,privacy-and-recovery,release-runbook,rollback}.md\"],\"data\":[\"release and recovery checklist\"],\"api\":[\"documented recovery boundary\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"deploying\",\"changing player saves\",\"support SLA\",\"legal approval\"],\"verification\":\"Cross-check review maps every recovery and release claim to a contract or marks it not run.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0005 and GATE-0007 remain explicit for policy and release authority.\",\"complexity\":\"low\",\"status\":\"ready_for_authoring\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0032\",\"title\":\"Create final PWA/release evidence hold audit\",\"domain\":\"quality\",\"targets\":[\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0011\",\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0001\",\"NFR-0003\",\"NFR-0006\",\"NFR-0009\",\"NFR-0011\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A final contract audit assembles implementation evidence requirements and records all unapproved release, browser, security, and provenance gates as holds rather than release approval.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0030\",\"IMP-0031\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"docs/release-evidence-hold-audit.md\",\"tests/release/evidence-audit*\"],\"data\":[\"final PWA/release evidence hold matrix\"],\"api\":[\"documented final-audit disposition\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"release approval\",\"deployment\",\"human sign-off impersonation\",\"gate resolution\"],\"verification\":\"Audit fixtures require every evidence row to be pass, fail, blocked, or not run with source and owner.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0002, GATE-0005, and GATE-0007 remain unresolved and block release claims.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"ready_for_authoring\"}\n  ],\n  \"expansion_queue\": [\n    {\"id\":\"SHARD-02\",\"title\":\"Campaign content and domain logic\",\"max_contracts\":250,\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\"],\"covers\":[\"exploration\",\"dialogue\",\"quests\",\"tutorial\",\"combat\",\"inventory\",\"party progression\",\"town/dungeon/ending content\",\"content validation\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0001\",\"REQ-0002\",\"REQ-0003\",\"REQ-0004\",\"REQ-0005\",\"REQ-0008\",\"NFR-0007\",\"NFR-0008\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0004\",\"target_allocation\":\"shared core and content only; no UI ownership\",\"state\":\"expanded\"},\n    {\"id\":\"SHARD-03\",\"title\":\"Session, UI, input, and accessibility\",\"max_contracts\":250,\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\",\"SHARD-02\"],\"covers\":[\"session/checkpoints\",\"semantic responsive shell\",\"game panels\",\"keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad adapters\",\"settings\",\"localisation\",\"captions\",\"feedback\",\"error recovery UI\",\"accessibility tests\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0005\",\"REQ-0006\",\"REQ-0007\",\"REQ-0009\",\"REQ-0010\",\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0003\",\"NFR-0004\",\"NFR-0005\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0002,GATE-0003,GATE-0004\",\"target_allocation\":\"shared UI model; web input/layout adapter; PWA inherits UI with no separate UI fork\",\"state\":\"expanded\",\"contract_count\":6},\n    {\"id\":\"SHARD-04\",\"title\":\"PWA delivery, performance, operations, and release evidence\",\"max_contracts\":250,\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\",\"SHARD-02\",\"SHARD-03\"],\"covers\":[\"PWA manifest/install\",\"service-worker cache lifecycle\",\"offline/update recovery\",\"performance measurement\",\"security headers\",\"release checks\",\"observability\",\"quality automation\",\"player/operator documentation\",\"platform certification assessment\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0011\",\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0001\",\"NFR-0003\",\"NFR-0006\",\"NFR-0009\",\"NFR-0011\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0002,GATE-0005,GATE-0007\",\"target_allocation\":\"web release build and PWA service-worker/install adapter are distinct; shared core owns neither cache nor hosting\",\"state\":\"expanded\",\"contract_count\":6},\n    {\"id\":\"SHARD-05\",\"title\":\"Connected-scope decision package\",\"max_contracts\":250,\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\"],\"covers\":[\"identity/sync conflict policy\",\"multiplayer/player safety\",\"live operations\",\"commerce/entitlements\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0014\",\"REQ-0015\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0006\",\"target_allocation\":\"no P0 target implementation; research/decision outputs only if explicitly authorised\",\"state\":\"hold\"}\n  ],\n  \"requirement_coverage\": {\n    \"REQ-0001\":\"queued: SHARD-02; provenance foundation IMP-0011\",\"REQ-0002\":\"queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0003\":\"queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0004\":\"queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0005\":\"queued: SHARD-02 and SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0006\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006, IMP-0007; queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0007\":\"current/gated: IMP-0010; queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0008\":\"current: IMP-0005, IMP-0011; queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0009\":\"queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0010\":\"current/gated: IMP-0010; queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0011\":\"queued: SHARD-04\",\"REQ-0012\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006, IMP-0009; queued: SHARD-03 and SHARD-04\",\"REQ-0013\":\"current: IMP-0002, IMP-0008\",\"REQ-0014\":\"gated: SHARD-05 / GATE-0006; no P0 implementation\",\"REQ-0015\":\"hold: SHARD-05 / GATE-0006; no P0 implementation\",\"NFR-0001\":\"queued: SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0002\":\"current/gated: IMP-0004, IMP-0006, IMP-0007\",\"NFR-0003\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006, IMP-0007; queued: SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0004\":\"current/gated: IMP-0010; queued: SHARD-03\",\"NFR-0005\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006; queued: SHARD-03\",\"NFR-0006\":\"current/gated: IMP-0009; queued: SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0007\":\"current: IMP-0005; queued: SHARD-02\",\"NFR-0008\":\"current: IMP-0005, IMP-0010, IMP-0011; queued: SHARD-02\",\"NFR-0009\":\"gated: SHARD-04 / GATE-0002\",\"NFR-0010\":\"current: IMP-0001, IMP-0002, IMP-0003, IMP-0004; queued target adapters in SHARD-03 and SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0011\":\"gated: SHARD-04 / GATE-0005\",\"NFR-0012\":\"current/gated: IMP-0001, IMP-0002, IMP-0003, IMP-0008, IMP-0012; queued: SHARD-04\"\n  },\n  \"dependency_graph\": {\"nodes\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\",\"IMP-0007\",\"IMP-0008\",\"IMP-0009\",\"IMP-0010\",\"IMP-0011\",\"IMP-0012\",\"IMP-0013\",\"IMP-0014\",\"IMP-0015\",\"IMP-0016\",\"IMP-0017\",\"IMP-0018\",\"IMP-0019\",\"IMP-0020\",\"IMP-0021\",\"IMP-0022\",\"IMP-0023\",\"IMP-0024\",\"IMP-0025\",\"IMP-0026\",\"IMP-0027\",\"IMP-0028\",\"IMP-0029\",\"IMP-0030\",\"IMP-0031\",\"IMP-0032\"],\"acyclic\":true,\"validation\":\"Each prerequisite points only to an earlier numbered contract; SHARD dependencies only point from later shards to earlier shards.\"}\n}\n# 04A \u2014 Original visual asset direction\n\nThis canonical P0 visual brief supplements the experience contract. It uses an original warm hand-painted fantasy style: readable silhouettes, worn clay and moss, lantern-gold highlights, plum shadows, rain-blue accents, restrained texture, and high-contrast semantic UI planes. It must not copy a reference game's characters, maps, sprites, UI, visual composition, or animation.\n\n## Required P0 families\n\n| Family ID | Purpose and required variants |\n| --- | --- |\n| `ASSET-ENV-TOWN` | Original hillside town: ground, boundaries, beacon states, interactables, readable daylight variants. |\n| `ASSET-ENV-DUNGEON` | Original Glassroot Hollow: floor/wall/exit language, collision markers, safe/locked/cleared states. |\n| `ASSET-CHAR-PARTY` | Original party silhouettes with idle, walk, battle-ready, and readable status states. |\n| `ASSET-CHAR-NPC` and `ASSET-ENEMY-HOLLOW` | NPC dialogue/avatar treatment plus a small original enemy roster with intent/status/defeated states. |\n| `ASSET-ITEM-INVENTORY` and `ASSET-UI-GAMEPLAY` | Labelled items and semantic UI icons/states for title, dialogue, quest, combat, save, settings, errors, and focus. |\n| `ASSET-FX-FEEDBACK` and `ASSET-PWA-IDENTITY` | Reduced-motion-safe optional feedback plus original PWA icons/manifest imagery. |\n\n## Provenance and accessibility\n\nEvery final asset receives a stable individual `ASSET-*` ID, creator/source record, originality/licence disposition, source/exported variants, and an owning R contract. Essential meaning must have a text, accessible-name, or non-colour equivalent. Asset tasks own content/provenance; PWA delivery owns hashing and caching. A family is complete only when original provenance, variants, responsive readability, and accessibility are verified.\n# 04B \u2014 Original audio direction and cue map\n\nThis canonical P0 audio brief requires original warm, lightly hand-played fantasy instrumentation with clear loops and modest dynamics. It must not reuse, imitate, sample, or reproduce recognisable melodies, arrangements, or sound identity from a reference game. Music, effects, and feedback are independently adjustable; non-text meaningful audio has captions/text equivalents and audio failure never blocks play.\n\n| Cue ID | Trigger | Loop / duration |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `AUDIO-MENU-LOOP` | Title, pause, and safe settings surfaces. | Seamless 30-second loop. |\n| `AUDIO-TOWN-LOOP` | Larkspur Reach exploration. | Seamless 45-second loop. |\n| `AUDIO-DUNGEON-LOOP` | Glassroot Hollow exploration. | Seamless 45-second loop. |\n| `AUDIO-BATTLE-LOOP` | Active turn-based combat. | Seamless 30-second loop. |\n| `AUDIO-VICTORY-STING` | Encounter/quest success. | One-shot, 2\u20134 seconds. |\n| `AUDIO-UI-FEEDBACK` | Focus, selection, unavailable action, confirmation. | One-shot, under 1 second. |\n| `AUDIO-SAVE-FEEDBACK` and `AUDIO-QUEST-FEEDBACK` | Save/recovery and objective/reward feedback. | One-shot, under 2 seconds. |\n| `AUDIO-ENDING-LOOP` | Beacon-restored ending. | Seamless 30-second loop. |\n\nEach cue must be allocated to an audio-required `IMP-*` and R contract with a stable `audio_id`, brief, duration, loop policy, trigger, mix category, caption/text equivalent, and originality review. Local generation still needs cue-level review for loop seams, clipping, trigger correctness, accessibility, and no recognisable reference melody.\n{\n  \"manifest_id\": \"mock-fantasy-quest-4-runbook-authoring-ledger\",\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"purpose\": \"Persistent